id: pm-s8ybl9
title: Read sessions emit invalid continuation identities from workspace activity rows
description: "The complete scale fixture now includes real schema workspace history. Context activity can contain the reserved _workspace identity, which the session producer copies into seen_item_ids although the strict session parser rejects that identifier. The following read fails with invalid_read_output_session. Keep non-item activity rows visible but exclude identifiers outside the existing portable item contract from reference-state accumulation; preserve strict validation and count-cap behavior."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-05T10:20:49.596Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-05T11:20:08.986Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-05T11:14:20.223Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-05T11:14:20.223Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: Every emitted next_state passes the unchanged strict session parser with workspace activity present; nonportable activity rows remain visible and are never replaced by invalid references; valid item identities retain suppression and capacity overflow behavior; full real context calibration observes the complete generated corpus and passes
parent: pm-4k6b
resolution: Exclude nonportable workspace activity identities from caller-carried item-reference state
expected_result: Every emitted continuation remains parseable and preserves visible workspace activity
actual_result: 32 output-session and contract tests pass; full calibrated context sessions round-trip with all 2243 source rows
